The portfolio has been acquired for $47.0 million (approximately $47 per square foot), which includes closing costs and the assumption of an aggregate of $34.5 million of existing debt. The mortgage debt, which is at a blended fixed interest rate of 6.56%, is fully amortizing over the remaining seven years, which is also the primary lease term of the supermarket leases ("Primary Term"). Acadia Acquisition invested $11.25 million of the equity capitalization.
