URL: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cme-group-inc-reports-all-time-record-revenue-adjusted-operating-income-adjusted-net-income-and-adjusted-earnings-per-share-for-q1-2025-302435191.html
CME Group Inc. Reports All-Time Record Revenue, Adjusted Operating Income, Adjusted Net Income and Adjusted Earnings Per Share for Q1 2025

 CME Group 

Apr 23, 2025, 07:00 ET

- Record revenue of $1.6 billion, up 10% from Q1 2024
- Record average daily volume (ADV) of 29.8 million contracts, with broad- based growth in every asset class

CHICAGO, April 23, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- CME Group Inc. (NASDAQ: CME) today reported financial results for the first quarter of 2025.

The company reported revenue of $1.6 billion and operating income of $1.1 billion for the first quarter of 2025. Net income was $956 million and diluted earnings per common share were $2.62. On an adjusted basis, net income was $1.0 billion and diluted earnings per common share were $2.80. Financial results presented on an adjusted basis for the first quarter of 2025 and 2024 exclude certain items, which are detailed in the reconciliation of non-GAAP results. 1 

"Amid heightened economic uncertainty, CME Group operated with exceptional resilience as clients turned to our markets in record numbers to hedge business risks across asset classes," said Terry Duffy, CME Group Chairman and Chief Executive Officer. "This increased demand drove our Q1 ADV to a new high of 29.8 million contracts and ... record revenue, adjusted operating income, ... for the quarter. Commodities grew 19%, ... increased 12%, and our ADV outside the U.S. reached a new high of 8.8 million contracts, up 19% year over year. Looking ahead, we remain focused on providing the products, services and efficiencies to benefit market participants as they navigate this risk-always-on environment."
