## Company Insight

 • Edelweiss Financial Services Limited (“EFSL”), was incorporated on November 21, 1995 under the name Edelweiss Capital Limited and started operations as an investment banking firm after receipt of a Category II license from SEBI. The name of Edelweiss Capital Limited was changed to ‘Edelweiss Financial Services Limited’ with effect from August 1, 2011. • The NCDs proposed to be issued under the Issue have been rated“Crisil A+/ Stable” (pronounced as “Crisil A plus rating” with stable outlook) for an amount of ₹12,000 million by Crisil vide their rating letter dated November 11, 2025, with rating rationale dated September 9, 2025. • EFSL has grown from a capital markets advisory business to a diversified financial services group engaged in businesses of asset management (alternatives and mutual funds), insurance (general and life insurance), asset reconstruction, credit (micro, small, micro enterprises and mortgages). • EFSL has a pan-India and international network with 252 (two hundred and fifty-two) domestic offices, and 3 (three) international offices (total 255 offices) and employed 5,764 as at September 30, 2025. • EFSL comprises 26 subsidiaries as at September 30, 2025. 

