[2] KLM Axiva Finvest Limited
URL: https://www.careratings.com/upload/CompanyFiles/PR/202601140122_KLM_Axiva_Finvest_Limited.pdf
Stable asset quality The company’s GNPA and Net NPA (NPA) stood at 1.99% and 1.12%, respectively, as on March 31, 2025, against 1.60% and 0.67% as on March 31, 2024. As on September 30, 2025, GNPA and NNPA marginally moderated to 2.21% and 1.19%, respectively. In absolute terms, GNPA increased to ₹33.23 crore as on March 31, 2025, from ₹27.53 crore as on March 31, 2024. Deterioration in asset quality was primarily attributable to the company’s exposure to relatively riskier asset classes such as business loans, MFI loans and unsecured personal loans. The 90+ days past due (DPD) levels are higher in MFI loan (19.68%), Personal loans (2.53%) and SME loans (1.07%), whereas lower in gold loans (0.79%) as on September 30, 2025. The company’s ability to improve the asset quality of its non-gold loan portfolio remains a key rating monitorable.

Key weaknesses 
Moderate profitability 
In FY25, KLM reported a profit after tax (PAT) of ₹20 crore on a total income of ₹341 crore against a PAT of ₹23 crore on a total 
income of ₹316 crore in FY24. The net interest margin (NIM) marginally declined to 8.22% in FY25 from 8.32% in FY24 due to 
high cash holding by the company. Operating expenses to average total assets increased to 7.35% in FY25 from 7.20% in FY24 
due to increase in advertisement and business promotion expense, while credit costs remained low at 0.27% in FY25. Owing to 
the increase in operating expenses, return on total average assets (ROTA) moderated to 1.05% in FY25 compared to 1.27% in 
FY24.
