Embassy Office Parks REIT, India’s first listed real estate investment trust and Asia’s largest office REIT by area, has successfully raised ₹2,000 crore through a 10-year non-convertible debenture (NCD) issuance — the first of its kind by an Indian REIT. The landmark issuance marks a significant step in the deepening of India’s REIT debt markets and underscores the strong credit standing Embassy REIT enjoys among long-term institutional investors. The NCDs, issued under Embassy REIT Series XV, carry a step-up coupon structure with an effective yield of 7.33%. The debentures will offer 7.25% for the initial five years and 7.45% for the subsequent five, with a put option at the end of the fifth year. The proceeds will be used to refinance existing debt and are expected to generate interest savings of around 70 basis points annually. 

 The issuance garnered strong interest from over 15 institutional investors, including life insurance companies, pension funds, and mutual funds, and was oversubscribed by 1.4 times. The long-tenor structure was particularly well-received by investors looking to deploy capital over extended horizons, aligning with their liability profiles.
