 market risk to which we are currently exposed, and, to which we expect to be exposed in the future, is interest rate risk. The face amount of our outstanding debt as of December 31, 2024 was $1.1 billion, of which $0.8 billion had a variable interest rate. Our primary sensitivity in 2024 was to changes in one-month Secured Overnight Financing Rate ("SOFR"), as the interest rates on our variable-rate indebtedness were based on this benchmark rate. We use interest rate swaps in order to maintain what we believe to be an appropriate level of exposure to interest rate variability. As of December 31, 2024, we held interest rate swaps related to $225 million of our variable-rate indebtedness. In addition, effective January 2, 2025, we have an additional $…
