## Project for NEOM

In the automated yard crane sector, Siemens has a new reference project for automated RTGs (ARTGs) at the Port of NEOM in Saudi Arabia. This greenfield terminal will feature 10 automated STS cranes and 30 ARTGs in the yard.

For NEOM, Siemens will integrate Mevea’s simulation technology into the crane automation system. Mevea’s simulators rely on physics-based Digital Twin technology. This will support assistive and autonomous system development and advanced training capabilities needed in operator training for the NEOM terminal.

Siemens now offers a “fully automated” RTG control system where only the final truck handling is “supervised”. The ARTG can gantry long travel automatically without operator control, but whether this is implemented depends on a risk assessment for the individual terminal.

