• The Cboe S&P 500 Zero-Cost Put Spread Collar Index (CLLZ) is designed to measure track the performance of a hypothetical low volatility strategy that (1) holds a long position indexed to the S&P 500 Index (SPX Index), (2) buys a monthly 2.5% Out-of-the-Money (OTM) SPX Put option to reduce the risk and sells a monthly 5% OTM SPX Put option (SPX Put Spread), and (3) sells a OTM monthly SPX Call option(s) to cover the cost of the Put spread. In particular, since the monthly SPX Call option is written to cover the cost of the SPX Put Spread, the strike of the SPX Call option is determined such that the premium (the last bid quote of the SPX Call option before 11:00 a.m. ET on the Cboe exchange) would equal the ask price of the 2.5% OTM SPX Put option minus the bid price of the 5% OTM SPX Put option. All options involved are AM-settled and roll on a monthly basis.
