Covered call delta is asset delta minus call delta because you wrote the call, while protective put delta is asset delta plus put delta because you bought the put and its delta is negative. With matching call and put terms, put-call parity makes those two position deltas equal, while asset plus short forward is approximately zero when matching asset and forward deltas are equal. A short call and short forward can look interchangeable because both subtract a delta. The supplied deltas give it away because an option delta is not generally the same as a forward delta, so compare those values before you call the positions equivalent.
