You will also see it called a protective collar, since the whole point is the floor it puts under your shares. A collar is what you get when you run a Covered Call and a Protective Put simultaneously on the same position:

- Own 100 shares of the underlying
- Sell 1 OTM call above the current price (the covered call leg, which caps upside and generates credit)
- Buy 1 OTM put below the current price (the protective put leg, which floors downside and costs premium)

