In order to examine the “naïve” put spread collar, we can rely on
the CBOE suite of strategy benchmark indexes and look to the
CBOE S&P 500 Zero-Cost Put Spread Collar Index (ticker CLLZ).
This index buys and sells one-month-to-expiry options, rolling
monthly, buying a 2.5% out-of-the-money (OTM) protective put,
selling a 5% OTM put, and selling an OTM call at a strike that
“pays for” the put spread.

