Role in strategic asset allocation

There are at least two interesting applications of this strategy in
a strategic asset allocation exercise: 1) risk-reduced equity and
2) “60/40” replacement (60% equity/40% bond) without explicit
rate sensitivity.

Risk-reduced equity. Our approach has demonstrated reliably
lower realized risk than equities alone—below, we see that the
rolling beta profile to equities is fairly consistent around the
long-term 0.57, notably dipping in the bear markets of 2002 and
the global financial crisis:

