Renowned investor and Ark Invest CEO, Cathie Wood, has defended the underperformance of the ARK Innovation ETF ARKK. Wood emphasized that the fund is dynamic and should not constitute a major part of any investment portfolio. Instead, she views it as part of a satellite strategy, which she believes aligns with current global trends.

The ARK Innovation ETF has seen a significant decline, losing nearly two-thirds of its value compared to its peak during the COVID-19 pandemic when meme stock mania propelled the price to nearly $160, resulting in a 149% surge in 2020. However, the fund has struggled since, raising doubts among investors about its strategy.

According to FactSet data, ARK Innovation has increased by only 2.8% this year, lagging behind the S&P 500's 24% rise. Over the past three years, the fund's price has averaged a decline of approximately 23% annually. Wood acknowledged that certain "interesting behaviors" during the pandemic contributed to the fund’s price surge but insists that the technologies and research backing her company's investments are highly advanced.

Wood identified the life sciences and healthcare sectors as primary drags on the fund. She expressed optimism that the emergence of new genomic therapy companies, like Intellia Therapeutics, offering alternative disease treatments, will improve the fund's performance.
