...
Two endpoint pairs cover Bitcoin and Ethereum ETF flows. `get_bitcoin_etf_flows_recent` and `get_bitcoin_etf_flows_all` both return a `data` array of daily records keyed by `Date`, with individual flow values for each of the 12 tracked tickers (IBIT, FBTC, BITB, ARKB, BTCO, EZBC, BRRR, HODL, BTCW, MSBT, GBTC, BTC) plus a `Total` column. The `_all` variant covers every trading day from January 2024 onward — a large response suitable for historical analysis — while `_recent` limits to the most recent trading days. Both return a `summary` object breaking down Fee, Total, Average, Maximum, and Minimum per ticker. The Ethereum counterparts (`get_ethereum_etf_flows_recent`, `get_ethereum_etf_flows_a…
