asset over time; (2) rising demand for hard-asset exposure as a hedge 
against inflation risk among institutional investors; and (3) the extremely 
limited and inelastic new supply of bitcoin.
We forecast bitcoin will be the best-performing institutional asset over 
the next decade, with its price rising to $1.3 million by 2035 (a 10-year 
forward compound annual growth rate of 28.3%). Those returns will 
come with significant volatility, though that volatility will be lower than 
historical averages.
