role as “digital gold” is central to its investment thesis.
In this regard, the most important macroeconomic factors to 
consider are those related to debt, deficits, and fiat currency 
debasement, as well as the role of the U.S. dollar as the world’s 
dominant reserve currency, as these play a role in institutional 
demand for gold-like assets. 
