Fortive’s Q2-25 results show modest top-line erosion and margin compression ahead of the Precision Technologies (PT) spin. Revenue slipped 2.2% YoY to $1.52 bn as softer product sales in PT (-5%) offset stable Intelligent Operating Solutions (IOS) and Advanced Healthcare Solutions (AHS). Gross margin eased 80 bp to 59.0%, while operating margin contracted 480 bp to 14.6% on $41 m separation costs and higher SG&A. Net earnings fell 14.6% to $166.6 m; diluted EPS dropped to $0.49 (vs $0.55).
...
- Revenue declined 2.2% YoY to $1.52 bn, with product sales down in two segments.
- Operating margin compressed 480 bp to 14.6% due to higher SG&A and separation costs.
- Diluted EPS dropped 11% YoY to $0.49, undershooting consensus expectations.
- Total debt increased to $4.81 bn; current portion surged to $1.91 bn, elevating near-term refinancing risk.
- Net earnings down 16% YTD, indicating sustained profit headwinds.
...
Revenue and EPS declines mirror a tougher macro and PT softness. Separation expenses obscured operating leverage, yet even stripping these out, margins declined ~180 bp. Cash bolstered by Ralliant dividend and strong working-capital management, but headline debt rose and $1.9 bn matures within 12 months, heightening near-term refinancing execution risk. Spin simplifies story and provides repurchase dry-powder, a shareholder-friendly use of proceeds. Overall, fundamentals look mixed: solid balance-sheet flexibility, but muted growth and margin pressure temper enthusiasm.
