## Cap your maximum trade loss at one or two percent of capital

The rule I follow is straightforward: never risk more than 1% to 2% of total account capital on a single trade setup.

To convert that rule into contract numbers, start with the maximum dollar risk formula:

`Max Dollar Risk = Total Account Value × Risk Percentage`

If a hypothetical account sits at $10,000 and the risk target is 1%, the absolute maximum loss budget for any new trade is $100.

