A vertical spread buys one option and sells another of the same type and expiry at a different strike — capping both your risk and your reward. This prices all four: bull call and bear put debit spreads, bull put and bear call credit spreads. Enter two strikes and your net premium to get max profit, max loss, risk/reward, break-even and a probability of profit from your implied volatility.
