thresholds below. 
FBAR 
U.S. persons, a group that includes citizens, resident aliens, trusts, estates, and domestic 
entities, with a financial interest in or signature authority over foreign financial accounts 
that exceed the threshold. This also reaches resident aliens of U.S. territories and territory 
entities.
