| Unmarried, or married filing separately — living abroad | $200,000 | $300,000 |
| Married filing jointly — living abroad | $400,000 | $600,000 |

Specified domestic entity $50,000 $75,000

Thresholds shown are for individuals. A specified domestic entity uses the U.S.-resident individual thresholds.

FBAR (one flat threshold) 
FBAR uses a single test: if the combined value of your foreign financial accounts exceeds 
$10,000 at any point during the calendar year, you must file. There's no separate threshold 
for residency or filing status, and the $10,000 is measured across all your foreign accounts 
added together, not account by account.
