## Tax treaties dataset coding book

Last updated: February 2021

This document gives a guide to the treaty provisions coded in the dataset, the coding rules followed, and the interpretation of some common non-standard wording. The dataset provides a simplified summary of certain parts of a treaty that may not fully reflect the detailed content. Always check the original treaty text.
...
• Each provision is coded in a purposive way. If within a treaty there is language that differs from the text of the UN model but would have the same or similar effect as a UN provision, it is coded as if the UN provision were present. This code book gives guidance for the most common variations. 
• Where treaty provisions are asymmetrical, they have been coded focusing on the taxing rights of the least developed country, as measured using GNI per capita on the date of signature. 
• Original treaties have been coded separately from subsequent amendments by protocol, which can also be found in the dataset. The exception is where an amending protocol and 

